# Archived memories

Retired 2026-09-01 by `memlint.py`, which found them contradicting current
reality. Not indexed by MEMORY.md, so nothing loads them at session start.
Kept rather than deleted because they are the record of how the machine used
to work.

- `project_memsearch_setup.md` — memsearch as a pip install with Milvus 2.6.4 in
  Docker on a Windows box. Now a uv tool at `~/.local/bin/memsearch`, and Milvus
  is not in the path at all. Superseded by the DEV memories
  `memory-compiler-pipeline`, `memsearch-index-path-drift`, `backup-sync-system`.
- `project-python-environment.md` — the Windows Python Install Manager toolchain.
  Superseded by Homebrew Python 3.14 under PEP 668 (`graphify-runtime-setup`,
  `path-shadowing-and-cleanup`).
- `user_context.md` — a full user profile that duplicated
  `~/.claude/global-memory/USER.md` and had both the job title and the operating
  system wrong.
